=== 3. THE PRE-CHECK -- HOW BIG IS THE SEASONAL ATMOSPHERIC d13C SIGNAL? ===
  A seasonal SST cycle modulates eps_up, which modulates the ISOTOPIC RATIO
  of the evasion limb only. For a sinusoid at omega = 2*pi/yr, well above the
  air-sea relaxation rate F_up/M_atm, the atmospheric response is
      amplitude(d13C_atm) = F_up * amplitude(eps_up) / (M_atm * omega)
  ⚠ ANALYTIC AND HEMISPHERICALLY LOCAL: it ignores interhemispheric exchange
    and the ocean's own d13C response, both of which DAMP it. So this is an
    UPPER bound on the term, which is the right side to err on for a gate
    whose purpose is to kill a mechanism.

  hem        F_up      M_atm  d eps/dT   amp eps | amp d13C_atm     OBSERVED    ratio
           GtC/yr        GtC  permil/K    permil |   permil p-p   permil p-p         
  NH        45.51     452.38   +0.1126    0.1203 |      0.00385       0.3567   0.0108
  SH        65.34     450.30   +0.1126    0.0605 |      0.00280       0.0337   0.0831

  stations: NH -> MLO, SH -> SPO (the two d13c_seasonal_* rows)
  GATE M: global atmosphere 902.7 GtC at 425.0 ppm ⇒ 2.1240 GtC/ppm vs the constant 2.1240 -> PASS


=== 3b. AGAINST THE ROWS' RESIDUAL -- WHICH IS WHAT sec.3's VERDICT ASKS FOR ===
  7 % of an OBSERVABLE is not the same statement as 7 % of what the model
  gets WRONG on that observable. And an amplitude alone cannot say whether a
  term helps: two vectors of the same size ADD or CANCEL by their PHASE.

  ⚠ THE RESPONSE PHASE IS DERIVED, NOT MEASURED. eps_up rises with SST, so
    the evasion limb sends ISOTOPICALLY HEAVIER carbon up in local summer;
    the atmosphere INTEGRATES that, so its anomaly lags the SST peak by a
    quarter cycle. The model's SST peaks at month 3.5 + CCX_SST_SEAS_LAG + 3
    in the NH and six months later in the SH (the sign flip at model.R:1421).

  hem       model     mo |   observed     mo |   RESIDUAL     mo |    omitted     mo |  |term|/
           permil        |     permil        |     permil        |     permil        |  |resid|
  NH       0.3463   9.52 |     0.3567   9.41 |     0.0240   1.31 |    0.00385  10.82 |    0.160
  SH       0.0643   3.12 |     0.0337   3.24 |     0.0307   2.99 |    0.00280   4.82 |    0.091

  and what the term would DO to each residual, added as a vector:
  NH   (MLO) residual 0.0240 -> 0.0253 permil  (+5.34 %)  phase gap -2.49 months ⇒ GROWS it
  SH   (SPO) residual 0.0307 -> 0.0324 permil  (+5.48 %)  phase gap +1.83 months ⇒ GROWS it


=== 4. SCORED ===
  the omitted term is 1.08 % (NH) / 8.31 % (SH) of the OBSERVED seasonal d13C.
  that is 1.1 orders of magnitude below the observable at its largest.
  against the ROWS' RESIDUAL it is 16.0 % (NH) / 9.1 % (SH).

  ⚠ SIGN ROBUSTNESS. The effect goes as |term| x cos(phase gap), so it flips
    at a gap of 3.00 months. The gaps and their margins:
      NH  gap -2.49 mo, 0.51 mo from the flip -> the sign is ⚠ MARGINAL
      SH  gap +1.83 mo, 1.17 mo from the flip -> the sign is robust

  ⇒ NOT THE EXPLANATION. The term is 9-16 % of what the model already 
    gets WRONG on the two rows that carry the veto, and at the derived phase 
    it moves both residuals the WRONG WAY by ~5 %. A flag worth -12.2 
    prior-sd cannot be paid for out of a term this size whichever way it 
    points. ⇒ IT IS REAL PHYSICS AND IT IS STILL NOT THE ANSWER -- which is 
      exactly the outcome handoff §5 said was worth an afternoon, not a refit.

  ⛔ AND THE MEAN VALUE IS A SEPARATE QUESTION FROM THE SLOPE -- see sec.5,
     which answers it from the same paper rather than from GLODAP.


=== 5. THE PAIR ITSELF -- §5a, ANSWERED FROM THE PAPER RATHER THAN FROM GLODAP ===
  ⭐ Having BOTH limbs measured makes this arithmetic. Zhang measures the
     KINETIC effect (both limbs carry it) and the EQUILIBRIUM DIC-gas offset
     (only the evasion limb also carries it), which is the structure Quay et
     al. 2003 eq.(2) uses. So the measured pair is
         eps_down = eps_k          eps_up = eps_k - eps_DIC-g
     and the steady state then puts d_ml - d_atm AT eps_DIC-g by construction.

  hem    eps_down      model |     eps_up      model |   d_ml-d_atm        model
  NH       -0.836      -2.00 |     -9.498     -10.00 |       +8.662        +8.00
  SH       -0.854      -2.00 |     -9.721     -10.00 |       +8.868        +8.00

  ⇒ the model's EVASION limb is nearly right and its INVASION limb is not:
     eps_up  -10.00 vs measured -9.498 / -9.721  -> off by 5-3 %
     eps_dn  -2.00 vs measured -0.836 / -0.854  -> 2.4x TOO LARGE
  ⚠ AND THAT RESOLVES THE TENSION THE FIRST PASS FLAGGED. It read the model's
    -10 as eps_up = -eps_DIC-g and concluded the pair needed eps_down ~ 0 to
    reproduce the equilibrium offset. With both limbs carrying eps_k the pair
    is consistent as it stands -- the model is simply 1.1 permil out on one
    limb and 1.2 out on the other, in the SAME direction, which is why its
    net offset (+8.00) is closer to right than either limb is.

  GATE Q -- Quay et al. 2003's OBSERVATIONAL constraint on that offset.
  Global mean air-sea d13C disequilibrium, 1995: 0.60 +- 0.10 permil.
    NH  d_ml  +0.719  d_atm  -8.013  ⇒ disequilibrium  +0.070 permil
    SH  d_ml  +0.746  d_atm  -7.970  ⇒ disequilibrium  -0.151 permil
    model global mean -0.040 vs observed 0.60 +- 0.10 -> ⛔ OUTSIDE 2 sigma
  ⚠ AN AREA-UNWEIGHTED TWO-BOX MEAN against a global observational estimate,
    and the model's own eps_DIC-g is used to define equilibrium -- so this
    tests the OFFSET the pair produces, not the pair's two limbs separately.

  ⭐ THE GATE HAS POWER BECAUSE THE QUANTITY IS UNSCORED. The ocean d13C
     stream is `ocean_grad_d13c`, a SURFACE-MINUS-DEEP gradient; the two
     d13c_level_* rows are ATMOSPHERIC. Nothing in the likelihood constrains
     the absolute surface-ocean d13C, so this is an independent test -- and
     a failure is an UNCONSTRAINED DIRECTION, not a broken fit.

  and it localises: holding d_atm and eps_DIC-g, the observed disequilibrium
    NH needs d_ml =  +1.249 permil; the model has  +0.719 -> -0.530 permil TOO LIGHT
    SH needs d_ml =  +1.497 permil; the model has  +0.746 -> -0.751 permil TOO LIGHT
  ⇒ THE GAP IS IN THE SURFACE d13C, NOT IN THE ALPHA PAIR: adopting the
    measured pair moves the offset by ~0.7 permil and the shortfall is ~0.6-0.8.
  ⚠ CANDIDATE, NOT A DIAGNOSIS: this mode's mixed layer is 139 m deep, well
    below a 50-75 m surface layer, and a deeper box mixes in lighter
    subsurface DIC. NOT TESTED HERE.
  ⛔ NOT A LICENCE TO RETUNE. It is a gate any adopted pair must still pass.


=== 6. WHAT ADOPTING THE MEASURED PAIR WOULD DO TO GATE Q ===
  ⛔ FIRST, A DEFECT THIS TEST HAD TO WORK AROUND AND THAT ANY ADOPTION MUST
     FIX: `alpha_as_down` / `alpha_as_up` are LITERALS inside ccx_prepare()'s
     aux (R/model.R:2023-2024) and are read from NOWHERE else. Setting them on
     a parameter list is a SILENT NO-OP -- it returns a number, unchanged, with
     no error. The first attempt at this section did exactly that and got four
     IDENTICAL rows, which is the only reason it was caught.
     ⇒ The one injection point is ccx_prepare() itself, patched below FOR THIS
       TEST ONLY so the SPINUP sees the new pair too -- the preindustrial
       isotopic equilibrium depends on it, and overriding after the spinup
       would start the run at the OLD equilibrium.

  hemispheric means of the measured pair: eps_down -0.845, eps_up -9.610
  (a SCALAR pair, as the model's is -- the hemispheric spread is carried as a
   residual below, not as two constants)

  model as it stands       d_ml +0.719/+0.746 | diseq +0.070/-0.151 mean -0.040 |  6.4 sigma ⛔ OUTSIDE
  measured pair (BOTH)     d_ml +1.473/+1.501 | diseq +0.850/+0.631 mean +0.741 |  1.4 sigma within 2
  invasion limb ONLY       d_ml +1.861/+1.889 | diseq +1.244/+1.024 mean +1.134 |  5.3 sigma ⛔ OUTSIDE
  evasion limb ONLY        d_ml +0.331/+0.359 | diseq -0.323/-0.544 mean -0.433 | 10.3 sigma ⛔ OUTSIDE

  ⭐ ONLY THE FULL PAIR WORKS. Either limb alone over- or undershoots, so this
     is not a knob being turned to meet a target -- it is two independently
     MEASURED constants that only agree with the observation together.
  ⇒ GATE Q goes from 6.4 sigma OUT WITH THE WRONG SIGN to 1.4 sigma.
  ⚠ AND IT IS STILL HIGH, not centred: the mean sits above the observation and
    the NH/SH spread is comparable to the observational sigma. NOTHING WAS
    REFITTED -- though note the fit has no direct handle here, since sec.5
    established that no stream scores this quantity.
  ⛔ ADOPTING THIS CHANGES THE OBJECTIVE ⇒ every fitted vector is quarantined
    and a refit is owed. That is the real cost and it should be batched with
    any other objective-changing adoption, not spent alone.

